    <string name="kojiki_wd_stall_text">DNS questions went unanswered for %1$d s; the tunnel engine was restarted to clear it.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_restart_title">DNS wedged — tunnel restarted</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_restart_text">Repeated DNS failures detected; the tunnel engine was restarted to clear them. If the wedge returns shortly, DNS will fail over to Google DoH.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_again_title">DNS wedged again — tunnel restarted</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_again_text">DNS failures persist on the fallback resolver; the tunnel engine was restarted again.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_failover_title">DNS failed over to %1$s</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_failover_text_temp">The tunnel restart did not cure the DNS wedge, so the resolver was switched from “%1$s” to “%2$s” and the tunnel was restarted. Temporary: “%1$s” is tried again in %3$d min.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_failover_text_manual">The tunnel restart did not cure the DNS wedge, so the resolver was switched from “%1$s” to “%2$s” and the tunnel was restarted. “%1$s” is not a DoH resolver, so switch back by hand.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_still_title">DNS still on %1$s</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_still_text">“%1$s” could not be found to switch back to; choose the resolver by hand.</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_back_title">DNS back on %1$s</string>
    <string name="kojiki_wd_back_text">The failover to %1$s was temporary; “%2$s” is in use again. If it wedges again soon, the next failover lasts longer.</string>
